WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.095
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:07.365 --> 00:08.935
Popcorn's almost ready!

3
00:09.155 --> 00:10.755
Fresh out of the pan, careful, it's hot!

4
00:14.945 --> 00:16.715
Yakisoba is ready!

5
00:18.285 --> 00:19.215
- Ah! - Good work!

6
00:19.215 --> 00:20.135
Thanks for your hard work!

7
00:20.159 --> 00:21.478
Hey, I'm here for a shift change!

8
00:22.285 --> 00:24.015
Huh? Where's Saeko?

9
00:24.445 --> 00:25.445
Hmm...

10
00:25.635 --> 00:28.195
Haven't seen her today yet.

11
00:28.425 --> 00:29.554
Huh?

12
00:29.555 --> 00:32.065
Did she seriously oversleep on day one of the festival?

13
00:32.445 --> 00:34.765
Why don't you give her a call?

14
00:35.585 --> 00:36.765
Oh, thanks.

15
00:36.895 --> 00:38.165
I'll call her in a bit.

16
00:39.165 --> 00:40.305
Let's go.

17
00:42.375 --> 00:43.705
Good work.

18
00:43.735 --> 00:44.974
Thanks, everyone!

19
00:44.975 --> 00:46.745
Miwa, have you seen Lucha?

20
00:47.795 --> 00:48.895
Haven't seen him.

21
00:49.385 --> 00:51.845
What the heck? Don't tell me he ditched his shift!

22
00:56.775 --> 00:58.825
If you mean Lucha, isn't that him over there?

23
01:05.355 --> 01:06.765
What's wrong with him?

24
01:07.995 --> 01:12.365
The girl he likes just came by to buy yakisoba.

25
01:12.795 --> 01:14.105
With her boyfriend, no less.

26
01:19.565 --> 01:23.375
Wonder if he can pull himself together before the headline act...

27
01:25.635 --> 01:27.215
By the way, where's Saeko?

28
01:28.055 --> 01:29.955
Looks like she's not here yet.

29
01:30.685 --> 01:33.555
Worst case, Saeko might have to fill in on vocals.

30
02:10.805 --> 02:18.305
"How Do We Relationship?"

31
02:23.798 --> 02:28.778
[Episode 6: Loving You, Having Loved You]

32
02:28.975 --> 02:30.935
Muscles! You definitely don't have enough muscle!

33
02:31.045 --> 02:33.215
Isn't it because you don't have enough muscle?

34
02:45.325 --> 02:46.795
- Look... - Um...

35
02:57.195 --> 02:58.395
About yesterday...

36
02:58.845 --> 02:59.945
I'm sorry.

37
03:01.875 --> 03:03.375
There's something...

38
03:03.945 --> 03:05.915
I have to tell you myself.

39
03:08.155 --> 03:09.655
I'm sorry too.

40
03:10.515 --> 03:11.625
Let's just

41
03:12.215 --> 03:13.485
lay everything out honestly.

42
03:14.185 --> 03:16.395
I've braced myself.

43
03:18.265 --> 03:21.025
Being honest with each other is what couples do, right?

44
03:24.235 --> 03:25.735
At the reunion...

45
03:26.565 --> 03:28.305
Nothing really happened.

46
03:30.175 --> 03:31.175
It's just...

47
03:32.375 --> 03:34.475
talking with senpai,

48
03:35.975 --> 03:37.375
I couldn't help remembering.

49
03:39.785 --> 03:40.945
Remembering what?

50
03:43.655 --> 03:44.855
That feeling back then...

51
03:44.925 --> 03:46.025
when my heart fluttered.

52
03:48.295 --> 03:49.295
I'm sorry.

53
03:51.095 --> 03:52.395
Back then...

54
03:53.965 --> 03:55.465
for a split second,

55
03:57.365 --> 03:59.765
I felt like... I might still like her...

56
04:03.535 --> 04:05.075
Yeah... And then?

57
04:05.555 --> 04:06.555
And then...

58
04:07.815 --> 04:08.815
But I...

59
04:09.975 --> 04:12.385
realized right away that it was totally wrong.

60
04:13.585 --> 04:16.155
I haven't contacted her since.

61
04:19.655 --> 04:23.124
Who tells their own girlfriend that they like another girl?

62
04:23.125 --> 04:24.395
You're honest to a fault.

63
04:27.735 --> 04:28.765
Well...

64
04:29.365 --> 04:30.365
Then again...

65
04:31.245 --> 04:34.805
I'm probably the idiot for pressing you when I already knew.

66
04:41.175 --> 04:42.815
You're mad, aren't you?

67
04:46.635 --> 04:48.215
I want to throw a fit, sure,

68
04:48.455 --> 04:50.785
but throwing a fit won't change anything.

69
04:54.955 --> 04:55.955
I'm sorry...

70
05:01.735 --> 05:02.735
Miwa.

71
05:03.425 --> 05:07.005
You chose me over her, right?

72
05:08.865 --> 05:09.675
Yeah.

73
05:09.875 --> 05:10.975
Yes, I did.

74
05:11.345 --> 05:12.575
Then we're fine.

75
05:13.545 --> 05:16.615
We've made up!

76
05:22.215 --> 05:23.985
What a relief...

77
05:25.285 --> 05:28.325
I was sure you were going to break up with me.

78
05:29.395 --> 05:32.224
I don't want to break up with you...

79
05:32.225 --> 05:35.195
Hey, don't cry.

80
05:37.905 --> 05:40.505
Now that I'm relieved, I just couldn't stop the tears...

81
05:45.175 --> 05:46.175
You know,

82
05:46.705 --> 05:49.275
I've never heard you say you like me.

83
05:51.245 --> 05:52.245
No way...

84
05:52.545 --> 05:53.645
I'm sure I have.

85
05:53.685 --> 05:56.585
Nope! Not once!

86
05:58.055 --> 05:59.355
Then I'll say it now...

87
06:00.085 --> 06:01.155
Don't bother.

88
06:01.295 --> 06:03.455
It doesn't count if you have to be coerced.

89
06:03.555 --> 06:04.695
Let's go.

90
06:09.695 --> 06:10.695
I like you.

91
06:11.145 --> 06:12.145
Saeko.

92
06:13.005 --> 06:14.005
I love you.

93
06:16.005 --> 06:18.075
That was... so half-assed!

94
06:18.105 --> 06:20.905
What was that? Zero emotion!

95
06:21.725 --> 06:23.024
You too, Saeko.

96
06:23.025 --> 06:24.944
You've never told me you like me either!

97
06:24.945 --> 06:27.224
Huh? Really?

98
06:27.225 --> 06:28.715
Say it then!

99
06:30.905 --> 06:32.185
I like you.

100
06:32.255 --> 06:36.295
I like you so, so much!

101
06:36.395 --> 06:39.295
Come on, Saeko, you're being just as half-hearted!

102
06:50.075 --> 06:51.635
It's all Lucha's fault anyway!

103
06:51.675 --> 06:53.704
Here we go, here we go!

104
06:53.705 --> 06:55.015
Ready, set, go!

105
06:55.075 --> 06:57.515
Hey, Miwa, don't just stand there filming!

106
06:57.815 --> 07:00.385
We are Lightning Rabbit!

107
07:00.485 --> 07:01.515
Rabbit!

108
07:01.855 --> 07:03.414
That's our Rika!

109
07:03.415 --> 07:04.785
So avant-garde!

110
07:08.305 --> 07:09.305
What is this?

111
07:09.455 --> 07:10.775
Hey, what is this supposed to be?

112
07:11.595 --> 07:12.865
It's a dragon!

113
07:14.835 --> 07:16.794
Pass it here. Miwa, you write something too!

114
07:16.795 --> 07:17.795
Here, here.

115
07:18.865 --> 07:20.665
Your turn, Miwa!

116
07:20.905 --> 07:22.705
What should I draw?

117
07:22.735 --> 07:23.735
Draw a dog.

118
07:23.905 --> 07:25.505
Oh, that's so cute!

119
07:25.605 --> 07:26.605
Super cute.

120
07:27.645 --> 07:29.075
I'm so beat!

121
07:30.515 --> 07:34.685
We don't have booth duty tomorrow, let's explore properly!

122
07:35.385 --> 07:36.855
Sounds good.

123
07:37.085 --> 07:38.954
I want to go to the haunted house!

124
07:38.955 --> 07:41.295
Um, the haunted house is a bit...

125
07:44.595 --> 07:45.825
Saeko.

126
07:47.085 --> 07:48.085
Um...

127
07:48.335 --> 07:50.565
You don't have work today, right?

128
07:50.965 --> 07:52.485
Want to stay over at my place tonight?

129
07:54.065 --> 07:55.575
Sure, but why all of a sudden?

130
07:56.105 --> 07:57.475
Well, no reason.

131
07:57.805 --> 07:58.805
Is that a no?

132
08:01.875 --> 08:02.875
Miwa.

133
08:03.245 --> 08:04.715
Do you like me?

134
08:06.785 --> 08:07.955
Again?

135
08:10.355 --> 08:11.455
Of course I do.

136
08:11.685 --> 08:12.685
I like you the most.

137
08:32.575 --> 08:33.845
What's wrong?

138
08:35.815 --> 08:37.375
Times like this,

139
08:37.515 --> 08:40.284
it really hits me that I'm dating a girl.

140
08:40.285 --> 08:41.855
And it feels really nice.

141
08:51.155 --> 08:53.595
It just hit me...

142
08:55.035 --> 08:59.235
I'm really so happy right now.

143
09:03.425 --> 09:05.875
Are you... really happy?

144
09:15.315 --> 09:16.315
Yeah.

145
09:17.705 --> 09:18.705
Because...

146
09:18.805 --> 09:20.155
not that long ago,

147
09:20.385 --> 09:24.195
I never even imagined I could actually get a girlfriend like this.

148
09:26.395 --> 09:28.795
So you're happy just because you get to date a girl?

149
09:31.465 --> 09:32.705
No, that's not it.

150
09:33.865 --> 09:36.805
It's because it's you, Saeko. That's why it's great.

151
09:37.465 --> 09:38.465
Because you're...

152
09:39.145 --> 09:41.975
so gentle, and such a wonderful person...

153
09:41.976 --> 09:43.945
You don't have to force yourself anymore.

154
09:46.885 --> 09:49.585
You're just trying to convince yourself, aren't you?

155
09:50.385 --> 09:53.465
You can't keep going unless you brainwash yourself into feeling happy, right?

156
09:55.705 --> 09:56.655
If this keeps up...

157
09:56.695 --> 09:57.925
I really can't take it.

158
09:58.765 --> 10:00.195
Actually... I've truly had enough.

159
10:02.865 --> 10:04.065
Saeko...?

160
10:08.235 --> 10:09.435
Let's break up.

161
10:10.235 --> 10:11.805
Please break up with me.

162
10:13.345 --> 10:14.345
No!

163
10:14.625 --> 10:15.934
I don't want to break up!

164
10:15.935 --> 10:17.175
Stay with me!

165
10:19.245 --> 10:20.415
Why are you doing this?

166
10:21.755 --> 10:23.214
Saeko, please!

167
10:23.215 --> 10:24.215
I like you!

168
10:25.725 --> 10:27.655
Hey, I really do like you!

169
10:28.855 --> 10:29.855
But...

170
10:30.425 --> 10:32.065
that's not romantic love at all.

171
10:35.335 --> 10:36.665
How can you say that...?

172
10:38.665 --> 10:40.205
You're too easy to read, Miwa.

173
10:41.105 --> 10:42.905
I can see right through you.

174
10:47.125 --> 10:48.975
Let's talk properly another day.

175
10:49.115 --> 10:51.005
Wait, don't go!

176
10:51.515 --> 10:52.614
Please...

177
10:52.615 --> 10:53.885
Just leave me alone.

178
11:03.705 --> 11:05.295
Fresh yakisoba, hot off the grill!

179
11:05.925 --> 11:07.725
Yakisoba available! Come get yours!

180
11:07.825 --> 11:10.065
Why is Saeko the one cooking?

181
11:10.535 --> 11:12.205
Weren't you on shift yesterday?

182
11:13.605 --> 11:14.964
Well...

183
11:14.965 --> 11:16.605
I was late yesterday.

184
11:16.775 --> 11:19.645
Skipped the first half, so I'm making up for it!

185
11:20.005 --> 11:21.275
I see...

186
11:21.915 --> 11:24.045
Is your band gonna be okay, though?

187
11:24.345 --> 11:25.345
Huh?

188
11:25.665 --> 11:28.315
Lucha's nursing a broken heart,

189
11:28.355 --> 11:31.755
and didn't Miwa call in sick today?

190
11:34.315 --> 11:35.315
Well...

191
11:35.425 --> 11:36.925
We'll manage somehow!

192
11:37.865 --> 11:41.225
By the way, if you're so free, help me bring in some customers!

193
11:41.435 --> 11:42.594
No way!

194
11:42.595 --> 11:44.805
Rika is off the clock right now!

195
11:45.705 --> 11:47.705
Hey, Rika!

196
11:47.905 --> 11:49.875
I'm swamped here!

197
12:38.625 --> 12:40.855
I'm all on my own...

198
12:45.665 --> 12:47.935
Saeko, you've gone down the slide way too many times.

199
12:47.965 --> 12:50.535
Yuria, don't you want to date someone?

200
12:50.865 --> 12:52.905
I do! Totally want to!

201
12:52.965 --> 12:54.064
Do you like anyone?

202
12:54.065 --> 12:55.134
Ever confessed to someone?

203
12:55.135 --> 12:56.474
Nope.

204
12:56.475 --> 12:58.575
Never confessed, never been confessed to.

205
12:59.045 --> 13:00.344
Makes sense.

206
13:00.345 --> 13:03.575
Being single is pretty common these days.

207
13:04.075 --> 13:06.035
Yeah...

208
13:08.215 --> 13:10.715
I used to think so too.

209
13:11.885 --> 13:15.355
But I still can't help feeling anxious.

210
13:16.255 --> 13:17.255
Anxious?

211
13:17.325 --> 13:18.325
Yeah.

212
13:19.455 --> 13:20.865
I keep feeling like

213
13:21.095 --> 13:24.905
maybe I'm the only person in the world who isn't loved by anyone.

214
13:32.975 --> 13:34.615
Whoa, wait! You startled me!

215
13:35.795 --> 13:36.795
Look at you!

216
13:37.555 --> 13:39.475
Sorry for getting so depressing all of a sudden.

217
13:42.005 --> 13:46.585
Even though I've dated, it's not like she truly loved me either.

218
13:46.925 --> 13:49.025
What? That's awful!

219
13:49.655 --> 13:52.395
Want me to beat up that ex-boyfriend for you?

220
13:52.535 --> 13:55.295
Wait, beating someone up is barbaric!

221
13:55.965 --> 13:56.965
Huh?

222
13:59.265 --> 14:00.965
Wait, is this why nobody wants me?

223
14:01.435 --> 14:02.935
Uh, how would I know?

224
14:05.705 --> 14:07.074
What a blow!

225
14:07.075 --> 14:08.945
Don't take it so hard!

226
14:23.475 --> 14:24.575
Actually...

227
14:25.775 --> 14:29.495
I don't blame her at all.

228
14:31.535 --> 14:35.605
She really is kind of a handful, though.

229
14:36.795 --> 14:39.045
Yet... she's so shy,

230
14:39.445 --> 14:40.905
and strangely earnest.

231
14:41.775 --> 14:43.315
Her head's full of romantic fantasies,

232
14:44.695 --> 14:48.015
and despite looking mature, she's like a kid on the inside.

233
14:49.315 --> 14:51.885
Everything's written on her face. She can't hide a thing.

234
14:54.355 --> 14:55.355
And yet...

235
14:56.455 --> 14:57.855
for some reason...

236
14:59.095 --> 15:01.465
all of that put together

237
15:03.065 --> 15:05.305
just made me adore her so much...

238
15:07.565 --> 15:08.735
Saeko...

239
15:14.205 --> 15:15.775
Though it's too late for all that now!

240
15:18.395 --> 15:21.855
Damn it!

241
15:34.735 --> 15:36.295
Screw this!

242
15:39.835 --> 15:41.735
I just wanted to be loved too...

243
16:23.615 --> 16:25.045
Hey, Saeko.

244
16:26.455 --> 16:27.555
Why?

245
16:29.685 --> 16:30.955
We were...

246
16:32.485 --> 16:34.585
getting along so well, weren't we?

247
16:37.535 --> 16:40.795
Were you, though? It felt pretty forced, didn't it?

248
16:42.135 --> 16:45.065
Honestly, it didn't look like you liked your girlfriend at all.

249
16:46.565 --> 16:48.135
That's not true...

250
16:48.335 --> 16:51.645
The one you really like is that senpai from before, isn't it?

251
16:52.405 --> 16:54.181
Have you ever felt your heart flutter for your current girlfriend

252
16:54.205 --> 16:57.145
the way it did for senpai?

253
16:58.445 --> 16:59.445
But...

254
16:59.985 --> 17:01.985
I have fun being with her.

255
17:02.055 --> 17:03.055
Yeah.

256
17:03.955 --> 17:06.185
And she's so kind.

257
17:07.255 --> 17:09.625
There's so much to look up to...

258
17:10.755 --> 17:12.095
I see.

259
17:12.195 --> 17:13.725
You're really fond of her.

260
17:15.765 --> 17:16.765
Yeah.

261
17:19.005 --> 17:20.005
And then what?

262
17:21.605 --> 17:23.835
Are you truly happy from the bottom of your heart?

263
17:36.815 --> 17:39.585
Sorry for bursting into tears like this.

264
17:40.355 --> 17:41.855
Annoying, right?

265
17:42.055 --> 17:44.565
Like I'm the tragic heroine of some drama.

266
17:44.575 --> 17:46.325
Not annoying at all!

267
17:47.025 --> 17:49.025
What's wrong with being the tragic heroine anyway?

268
17:50.365 --> 17:53.805
Besides, people are supposed to cry when they're sad.

269
18:00.195 --> 18:01.615
That's true...

270
18:02.315 --> 18:03.945
It's okay to cry, right?

271
18:06.855 --> 18:08.014
Hey, Saeko!

272
18:08.015 --> 18:09.331
Want to go blow off some steam at karaoke?

273
18:09.355 --> 18:11.884
But with the festival tomorrow, I might have to sing on stage.

274
18:11.885 --> 18:14.825
Man, I really want some yakisoba too!

275
18:15.125 --> 18:16.131
I'll make you some next time.

276
18:16.155 --> 18:17.395
Wait, really?

277
18:26.305 --> 18:28.375
Saeko smiling so brightly like that...

278
18:31.355 --> 18:36.675
when was the last time I saw [her like that]?

279
18:54.835 --> 18:58.005
Anyway... let's just break up.

280
18:58.405 --> 18:59.405
That's all.

281
19:04.035 --> 19:07.145
Don't look like it's the end of the world.

282
19:08.955 --> 19:09.955
Because...

283
19:11.075 --> 19:14.885
it's my first breakup ever.

284
19:15.415 --> 19:17.314
We're just going back to being friends.

285
19:17.315 --> 19:19.025
Just be natural, like we always are.

286
19:21.455 --> 19:22.525
That's true.

287
19:22.925 --> 19:23.925
I'm sorry...

288
19:24.025 --> 19:25.924
I told you to stop apologizing!

289
19:25.925 --> 19:27.495
No more "I'm sorry"!

290
19:44.345 --> 19:47.415
Want to watch some funny clips?

291
19:49.055 --> 19:50.515
Funny clips...?

292
19:53.585 --> 19:54.585
Ah.

293
19:54.695 --> 19:55.795
This one, look!

294
20:03.195 --> 20:04.494
Wait, play it again!

295
20:04.495 --> 20:05.605
Again?

296
20:08.915 --> 20:10.535
It's so dumb, but hilarious, right?

297
20:21.755 --> 20:22.755
What's wrong?

298
20:25.185 --> 20:26.185
Nothing.

299
20:27.275 --> 20:28.275
I just felt like...

300
20:29.995 --> 20:32.565
it's been a while since I saw you smile.

301
20:33.025 --> 20:36.765
Wait, am I usually that stone-faced?

302
20:37.935 --> 20:39.265
Even if you say that...

303
20:43.275 --> 20:46.305
you really never looked at me, did you, Miwa?

304
20:51.385 --> 20:52.685
You're right...

305
21:02.995 --> 21:04.195
That look in your eyes...

306
21:04.925 --> 21:07.865
I absolutely despise it...

307
21:10.855 --> 21:11.855
Ouch!

308
21:13.895 --> 21:15.805
Come on, our set's starting soon!

309
21:15.835 --> 21:17.375
Pull yourself together!

310
21:30.895 --> 21:32.425
Still not working, huh...

311
21:35.295 --> 21:37.495
Pull this again and you're fired!

312
21:38.625 --> 21:39.765
I'm sorry...

313
21:42.195 --> 21:43.265
Whatever.

314
21:43.795 --> 21:46.505
I felt like screaming my lungs out anyway!

315
21:48.515 --> 21:49.605
All right!

316
21:49.675 --> 21:50.735
Let's do this, everyone!

317
21:53.105 --> 21:54.105
Come on.

318
21:54.145 --> 21:55.145
You too, Lucha!

319
21:56.815 --> 21:58.585
How long are you gonna keep crying?

320
21:59.445 --> 22:00.445
Hands in!

321
22:00.685 --> 22:01.685
Let's go!

322
22:03.175 --> 22:04.175
Yeah!

323
22:05.725 --> 22:06.725
Yeah!

324
22:08.255 --> 22:13.395
Lightning Rabbit, go!

325
22:27.105 --> 22:32.315
♪ Hey, if the world were to end today, ♪

326
22:32.485 --> 22:37.685
♪ who would you choose to have by your side? ♪

327
22:38.195 --> 22:40.054
♪ Hey, whether it's music ♪

328
22:40.055 --> 22:43.454
♪ or your favorite chocolate cake, ♪

329
22:43.455 --> 22:45.594
♪ I'll be waiting for you right here. ♪

330
22:45.595 --> 22:47.195
♪ So look at me. ♪

331
22:49.115 --> 22:54.235
♪ If you had shown me your tears back then, ♪

332
22:54.265 --> 22:58.205
♪ whether time or love, ♪

333
22:58.215 --> 23:00.104
♪ I would've poured it all into you. ♪

334
23:00.105 --> 23:05.585
♪ Until this day comes to an end, ♪

335
23:05.595 --> 23:08.614
♪ please take my hand ♪

336
23:08.615 --> 23:11.325
♪ as if nothing had ever happened. ♪

337
23:11.355 --> 23:16.594
♪ Even when tomorrow arrives, ♪

338
23:16.595 --> 23:19.494
♪ please tell me everything is just the same. ♪

339
23:19.495 --> 23:23.635
♪ Because this dream will never end, ♪

340
23:24.515 --> 23:29.105
♪ no matter how long, we'll always be together. ♪

341
23:50.695 --> 23:52.565
[Next Episode Preview] It's already been a month since we broke up.

342
23:52.575 --> 23:54.665
We were supposed to be strangers again.

343
23:54.765 --> 23:55.974
We're bandmates!

344
23:55.998 --> 23:56.998
Bandmates...?

345
23:57.765 --> 23:58.835
Let's go!

346
23:58.865 --> 24:00.754
So greedy and selfish.

347
24:00.755 --> 24:02.955
There's something really off about you right now, Miwa.

348
24:03.255 --> 24:04.775
Shiho senpai.
